          "author_association": "OWNER",
          "body": "## Purpose\n\nDisposable native acceptance for #317. The owner authorizes the bounded fixture implementation below and integration assessment of its completed candidate. The fixture must never be merged. Label admission, deliberate stale-intent rejection and recovery will be orchestrated separately by the owner; they are not extra implementation tasks.\n\n## Implementation scope\n\nAdd `docs/process/issue-317-integration-fixture.md` containing exactly one heading, `# Integration assessment fixture`, and the paragraph `This disposable candidate exercises authenticated integration assessment without merge permission.` Create the normal docs-only OpenSpec proposal, design and completed tasks for this issue, using `skip_specs: true` and a current provider-emitted evidence-contract citation. Preserve every unrelated file and the canonical product and architecture models.\n\nThe host independently installs dependencies, runs repository verification and strictly validates the OpenSpec change before publication. Avoid duplicating a full dependency installation and repository verification inside the agent solely for this small documentation fixture; inspect the existing provider conventions and return the completed candidate for fresh independent host checks. Do not invent passed checks or block the candidate on later owner-orchestrated acceptance steps.\n\n## Acceptance and boundaries\n\n- One fixture document and this issue's completed OpenSpec plan, delivered together in one implementation PR.\n- Independent host checks and required CI pass; the candidate becomes ready.\n- The owner will separately exercise an integrate request without prerequisites, current-head approval under a human reservation, a deliberately invalidated integration request, and a final successful assessment with `merge: false`.\n- No product change, merge, release or deployment is authorized for this disposable candidate. The issue and PR will be closed without merging after the observations are retained.",
